  description: Lawrencium is a synthetic chemical element with chemical symbol Lr
    (formerly Lw) and atomic number 103. It is named in honor of Ernest Lawrence,
    inventor of the cyclotron, a device that was used to discover many artificial
    radioactive elements. A radioactive metal, lawrencium is the eleventh transuranic
    element and is also the final member of the actinide series.
